      "question": {
        ":question/id": "afe8ca44-fa0e-5554-b280-8bb7e7c4a168",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "Given that $A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & x & -3 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $det(A)=-11$, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Expand along the first row, using the signs $+,-,+$. Compute the three signed contributions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{1} & =(2)\\begin{vmatrix}x & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(2)((x)(1)-(-3)(5)) \\\\  & =(2)(x + 15) \\\\  & =2 x + 30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{2} & =-(1)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =-(1)((3)(1)-(-3)(1)) \\\\  & =-(1)(6) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T_{3} & =(0)\\begin{vmatrix}3 & x \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =(0)((3)(5)-(x)(1)) \\\\  & =(0)(15 - x) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdd the signed contributions to obtain the determinant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =T_1+T_2+T_3 \\\\  & =2 x + 24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSet the determinant equal to the given value.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 x + 24 & =-11 \\\\ 2 x & =-35 \\\\ x & =- \\frac{35}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=- \\frac{35}{2}$.",
